# Skill eval sets are hand-maintained and kept in a compact style: one
# {"text": "..."} assertion per line. Prettier's default JSON printer expands
# each of those onto three lines, which turns a four-eval addition into a
# ~300-line diff and destroys blame on the file. Formatting here is deliberate.
skills/*/evals/*.json

# The Kaizen template is byte-sensitive. `template_hash` on every kaizen note is
# a sha256 over the file's raw bytes (src/kaizen/loader.ts), and a review
# reproduces template prose into the note byte-for-byte. Prettier collapses the
# bandwidth table's column padding, which changes the hash — so notes stop
# tracing back to the template version that produced them, and the re-padded
# table lands in the review itself.
templates/kaizen.md

# Task lists are inputs to an automated runner (the `sab.tasks/1` schema, read by
# saboteur-feature-orchestrator and the tasks.md import). Prettier inserts blank
# lines between fields and rewrites emphasis (*later* -> _later_) inside prose
# that is meant to be preserved as written.
Docs/feature-specs/**/tasks.md
Docs/feature-specs/**/*-tasks.md

# Build output
dist/
ui/dist/
